diff --git a/docs/upgrades/0.4.0.md b/docs/upgrades/0.4.0.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..788b9c94
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/upgrades/0.4.0.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Upgrading to Naive 0.4.0: the structured layout
+
+0.4.0 gives a venture three folders at the top, each with one job (EE-086):
+
+```text
+my-venture/
+  venture.json  README.md  AGENTS.md
+  knowledge/    the knowledge base: foundation/, product/, customers/, people/, money/, decisions/ ...
+  meta/         sources.json, naive.config.json, provenance.jsonl, releases/
+  repo/         optional: the code base
+```
+
+New ventures start in this layout. An existing venture moves when you ask, because the move touches every folder. Run `naive upgrade --layout structured --check` to see what would move, then `naive upgrade --layout structured` (add `--owner <person>` to name the owner of every function):
+
+- Every package folder and record at the top moves into `knowledge/`.
+- `provenance.jsonl`, `naive.config.json` and `knowledge/sources.json` move into `meta/`, and `.release/` becomes `meta/releases/`.
+- `profile.md` becomes `README.md`.
+- `venture.json` gains `"layout": "structured"` and a flat org chart in `functions`: one function per package, owned by `--owner`, or by you if `people/` says you are building solo.
+
+Nothing you cite changes. Every record keeps its route (`foundation/problem` is still `foundation/problem`), so no alias is needed, and the provenance log reads the same. Files git tracks move with `git mv`, so their history follows them.
+
+After upgrading:
+
+- **On a team**, name each function's owner in `venture.json` under `functions`. People's hats are read from there now, and `people/people.json` no longer stores them.
+- **To combine functions**, declare one that lists several packages, such as `"growth": { "packages": ["marketing", "customers", "money"], "owner": "you" }`.
