+## Move to the structured layout
+
+Naive 0.4.0 gives a venture three folders at the top: `knowledge/` for the knowledge base, `meta/` for what Naive keeps about it, and an optional `repo/` for code ([Project structure](./project-structure)). New ventures start there. An existing venture moves when you ask, because the move touches every folder:
+
+```sh
+node interface/cli/mentura.mjs init ~/ventures/layout-demo --id layout-demo
+node interface/cli/naive.mjs upgrade ~/ventures/layout-demo --layout structured --check
+node interface/cli/naive.mjs upgrade ~/ventures/layout-demo --layout structured --owner the-founder
+node schema/structure.mjs ~/ventures/layout-demo
+```
+
+`--check` lists what would move and changes nothing. The upgrade moves every package into `knowledge/`, moves `provenance.jsonl`, `naive.config.json`, `sources.json` and `.release/` into `meta/`, and renames `profile.md` to `README.md`. It writes a flat org chart into `venture.json`, one function per package, owned by `--owner` or by the solo founder `people/` names. Files git tracks move with `git mv`, so their history follows them.
+
+Routes do not change. `foundation/problem` is still `foundation/problem`, so no alias is needed, and citations and the provenance log read the same.
+
 ## Read the guide for each version
 
 Each framework version has a guide in `docs/upgrades/`, read from the copy of Naive you have installed. It says what the migrations do and what is left for you to do by hand:
